[{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q1","number":1,"question":"<p><strong>The following exercise uses Hyperbolic Functions and requires Integration methods from A-Level Further Maths</strong></p><p>Two points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lie on the curve given. In each case the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are given along with the curve. Find the exact length of the arc <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"PQ\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_P=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_Q=35\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac23x^{3/2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_P=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_Q=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac43x^{3/2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac23x^{3/2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=\\sqrt{x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_8^{35}\\sqrt{1+x}\\,dx\n=\\left[\\frac23(1+x)^{3/2}\\right]_8^{35}\n=144-18=126\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac43x^{3/2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=2\\sqrt{x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_1^4\\sqrt{1+4x}\\,dx\n=\\left[\\frac16(1+4x)^{3/2}\\right]_1^4\n=\\frac{17\\sqrt{17}-5\\sqrt5}{6}\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>The diagram below shows the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\cosh x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.37/questions/assets/FMQ_2.37_q2_diagram_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinates 2 and 3 respectively. Show that the arc length of the curve from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is equal to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac7{12}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\cosh x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=\\sinh x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{1+\\sinh^2x}=\\cosh x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Using the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-coordinates stated in the question,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_2^3\\cosh x\\,dx=[\\sinh x]_2^3=\\sinh3-\\sinh2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q3","number":3,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int\\sec x\\,dx=\\ln|\\sec x+\\tan x|\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol><p>A curve is given for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac\\pi4\\leq x\\leq\\frac\\pi3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> by the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\ln(\\cos x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>[b)] Find the length of the arc on this curve, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ln\\left(\\frac pq\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are exact irrational numbers.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\sec x\\,dx\n =\\int\\frac{\\sec^2x+\\sec x\\tan x}{\\sec x+\\tan x}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\ln|\\sec x+\\tan x|+c,\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>since the numerator is the derivative of the denominator.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\ln(\\cos x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=-\\tan x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and the speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{1+\\tan^2x}=\\sec x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on the given interval. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns =\\int_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/3}\\sec x\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\left[\\ln|\\sec x+\\tan x|\\right]_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/3}\n=\\ln\\left(\\frac{2+\\sqrt3}{1+\\sqrt2}\\right)\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>A curve is given by the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac12x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the exact length of the arc on the curve, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, between the origin and the point where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Here <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^2\\sqrt{1+x^2}\\,dx.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sinh u\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx=\\cosh u\\,du\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The limits are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\operatorname{arsinh}2=\\ln(2+\\sqrt5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns =\\int_0^{\\ln(2+\\sqrt5)}\\cosh^2u\\,du\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\left[\\frac u2+\\frac14\\sinh2u\\right]_0^{\\ln(2+\\sqrt5)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\sqrt5+\\frac12\\ln(2+\\sqrt5)\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>A curve is given by the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\\cosh\\left(\\frac y2\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the exact length of the arc on the curve, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, between the points where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\ln4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx/dy=\\sinh(y/2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the arc length is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^{\\ln4}\\sqrt{1+\\sinh^2(y/2)}\\,dy\n=\\left[2\\sinh(y/2)\\right]_0^{\\ln4}\n=\\frac32\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Part of a suspension bridge is shown in the diagram below, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are directly beneath <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.37/questions/assets/FMQ_2.37_q6_diagram_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>It is given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"PO=OQ=70\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AP=CQ=40\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres. Point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is 15 metres above <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The cable that runs from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> can be modelled by the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=k\\cosh\\frac{x}{k}-p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k-p=15\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Use part (a) to verify that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=101.91\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to two decimal places.</p></li><li><p>Find the length of the cable, from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, to the nearest metre.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The cable passes through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B=(0,15)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15=k\\cosh0-p=k-p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>From part (a), <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=k-15\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(70,40)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n40=k\\cosh\\left(\\frac{70}{k}\\right)-(k-15),\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(k)=k\\cosh(70/k)-k-25=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Evaluating near the root gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(101.905)&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(101.915)&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is continuous, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=101.91\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to two decimal places.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=101.91\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=86.91\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the gradient is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=\\sinh(x/101.91)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns =\\int_{-70}^{70}\\sqrt{1+\\sinh^2(x/101.91)}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\left[101.91\\sinh(x/101.91)\\right]_{-70}^{70}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\approx151.271=151\\text{ m to the nearest metre}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Two masts, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, are built 500 metres apart on horizontal ground. A wire is hung between the masts so that its shape can be modelled by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny=p+\\cosh\\left(\\frac{x}{q}-r\\right)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the height in metres of the wire above the ground, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the distance in metres from mast <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive constants. The diagram below shows the model as being hung from the very top of the mast, which is at a height of 80 metres, and that the minimum distance between the ground and the wire is 60 metres.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.37/questions/assets/FMQ_2.37_q7_diagram_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and hence find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to three significant figures.</p></li><li><p>Find the length of the wire hung between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to the nearest metre.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The minimum occurs at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=250\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and has height <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"60\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p+1=60\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=59\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At the minimum, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"250/q-r=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=80\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cosh r=21\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\operatorname{arcosh}21=\\ln(21+2\\sqrt{110})\\approx3.74,\n\\qquad q=\\frac{250}{r}\\approx66.9.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Using the unrounded values <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\\approx66.897\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\\approx3.7371\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the arc length is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^{500}\\sqrt{1+\\left(\\frac1q\\sinh\\left(\\frac{x}{q}-r\\right)\\right)^2}\\,dx\n\\approx503.225=503\\text{ m to the nearest metre}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>Two poles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"CD\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are placed in the ground, 3 metres apart from each other, as shown in the diagram below. The height of the pole <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is 1.5 metres.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/2.37/questions/assets/FMQ_2.37_q8_diagram_v01.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>A rope is attached to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the tops of the two poles, and hangs so that it touches the ground at point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, which is 1.6 metres from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The curve is modelled using the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ny=p\\cosh(qx-r)-2\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive constants.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and hence find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to four significant figures.</p></li><li><p>Find the height of pole <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"CD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to the nearest centimetre.</p></li><li><p>Find the length of the rope between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer to the nearest centimetre.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The curve reaches its minimum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p-2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.6q-r=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=1.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cosh r=1.75\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\operatorname{arcosh}(1.75)\\approx1.15881,\n\\qquad q=\\frac{r}{1.6}\\approx0.7243.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Substituting <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2\\cosh(0.724256\\cdot3-1.15881)-2\\approx1.11927\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"CD=1.12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m to the nearest centimetre.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Using the rounded parameters in the model, numerical integration gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns =\\int_0^3\\sqrt{1+\\left(1.44851\\sinh(0.724256x-1.15881)\\right)^2}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n \\approx4.1795=4.18\\text{ m to the nearest centimetre}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>For each of the following, find the length of the arc, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, on the given curve between the origin and the point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer in terms of the constant, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1k\\cosh^2(kx)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1k\\sinh^2(kx)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1k\\cosh^2(kx)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=\\sinh(2kx)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^1\\sqrt{1+\\sinh^2(2kx)}\\,dx\n=\\left[\\frac{1}{2k}\\sinh(2kx)\\right]_0^1\n=\\frac{\\sinh(2k)}{2k}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac1k\\sinh^2(kx)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=\\sinh(2kx)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as well. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^1\\sqrt{1+\\sinh^2(2kx)}\\,dx\n=\\frac{\\sinh(2k)}{2k}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q10","number":10,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>By using the substitution <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac16\\sinh u\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\sqrt{1+36x^2}\\,dx=\\frac1{12}\\operatorname{arsinh}(6x)+\\frac12x\\sqrt{1+36x^2}+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol><p>Hence calculate the exact length of the arc on the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> between the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac16\\sinh u\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx=\\frac16\\cosh u\\,du\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{1+36x^2}=\\cosh u\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\sqrt{1+36x^2}\\,dx\n =\\frac16\\int\\cosh^2u\\,du\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac1{12}u+\\frac1{24}\\sinh2u+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac1{12}\\operatorname{arsinh}(6x)+\\frac12x\\sqrt{1+36x^2}+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=3x^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=6x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns =\\int_0^{1/3}\\sqrt{1+36x^2}\\,dx\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\left[\\frac1{12}\\operatorname{arsinh}(6x)+\\frac12x\\sqrt{1+36x^2}\\right]_0^{1/3}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac1{12}\\ln(2+\\sqrt5)+\\frac{\\sqrt5}{6}\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q11","number":11,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>By using substitution <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sinh^2u\" data-display=\"false\"></span> show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\sqrt{\\frac{x+1}{x}}\\,dx=\\sqrt{x(x+1)}+\\operatorname{arsinh}\\sqrt{x}+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol><p>Hence calculate the exact length of the arc, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, on the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac23\\sqrt{x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> between the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving your answer in logarithmic form.</p>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sinh^2u\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx=2\\sinh u\\cosh u\\,du\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\sqrt{\\frac{x+1}{x}}\\,dx\n =\\int2\\cosh^2u\\,du=u+\\frac12\\sinh2u+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\operatorname{arsinh}\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{x(x+1)}+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac23\\sqrt{x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=1/(3\\sqrt{x})\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. With <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=9x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns =\\int_1^4\\sqrt{1+\\frac1{9x}}\\,dx\n=\\frac19\\int_9^{36}\\sqrt{\\frac{u+1}{u}}\\,du\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac19\\left[\\operatorname{arsinh}\\sqrt{u}+\\sqrt{u(u+1)}\\right]_9^{36}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac19\\ln\\left(\\frac{6+\\sqrt{37}}{3+\\sqrt{10}}\\right)+\\frac{2\\sqrt{37}}3-\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}3\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>A curve is given by the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=5-\\ln(1-x^2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the exact length of the arc on the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int\\left(\\frac{1+x^2}{1-x^2}\\right)dx.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li><li><p>Hence the exact length of the arc on the curve between the points where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=5-\\ln(1-x^2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2x}{1-x^2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n1+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right)^2\n =\\frac{(1-x^2)^2+4x^2}{(1-x^2)^2}\n=\\frac{(1+x^2)^2}{(1-x^2)^2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For the stated interval, the arc-length integrand is therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1+x^2)/(1-x^2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Using partial fractions,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{1+x^2}{1-x^2}=-1+\\frac1{1-x}+\\frac1{1+x}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\left[-x-\\ln(1-x)+\\ln(1+x)\\right]_0^{1/2}\n=\\ln3-\\frac12\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>A landscape gardener is designing a curved path which will be exactly 39 metres long. The edge of the path follows the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac13x^{3/2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are measured in metres. By considering the origin as the start point of the curve, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which gives a length of 39 metres.</p>","steps":["<p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac13x^{3/2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dy/dx=\\frac12\\sqrt{x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns =\\int_0^k\\sqrt{1+\\frac{x}{4}}\\,dx\n=\\left[\\frac13(4+x)^{3/2}\\right]_0^k\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac13(4+k)^{3/2}-\\frac83.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Setting <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=39\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4+k)^{3/2}=125\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4+k=25\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=21\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>Engineers are designing the shape of a suspension bridge cable. The cable hangs between two supports and its height above the road can be modelled by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nh=a+\\cosh\\left(\\frac xb-c\\right)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the height of the cable above the road (in metres), <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the horizontal distance from one end of the bridge (in metres), and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants. The bridge span is 60 m long (horizontally), so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq x\\leq60\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The lowest point of the cable occurs at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=30\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where the height is 12 metres. The cable height at each end of the bridge is 20 metres.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer in exact form.</p></li><li><p>Hence, using your calculator, find the length of the cable used giving your answer to the nearest metre.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The minimum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=30\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30/b-c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12=a+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=11\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20=11+\\cosh c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nc=\\operatorname{arcosh}9=\\ln(9+\\sqrt{80}),\\qquad\nb=\\frac{30}{\\ln(9+\\sqrt{80})}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dh/dx=b^{-1}\\sinh(x/b-c)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, numerical integration gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^{60}\\sqrt{1+\\frac1{b^2}\\sinh^2\\left(\\frac xb-c\\right)}\\,dx\n\\approx63.448=63\\text{ m to the nearest metre}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>A curve for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=t^2,\\quad y=\\frac13t^3-t.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2=(t^2+1)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence find the exact length of the curve between the points that occur when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=2t,\\qquad \\frac{dy}{dt}=t^2-1.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2\n=4t^2+(t^2-1)^2=(t^2+1)^2.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^4\\sqrt{(t^2+1)^2}\\,dt\n=\\int_0^4(t^2+1)\\,dt\n=\\left[\\frac13t^3+t\\right]_0^4\n=\\frac{76}{3}\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by the parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=\\frac23t^3+2,\\quad y=2\\sqrt2\\,t^2+1\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the arc length between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=\\int_0^2 2t\\sqrt{t^2+k}\\,dt\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for a constant value <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence find the exact length of the arc of the curve between the points where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=2t^2,\\qquad \\frac{dy}{dt}=4\\sqrt2\\,t.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2\n =4t^4+32t^2=4t^2(t^2+8),\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns =\\int_0^2\\sqrt{4t^2(t^2+8)}\\,dt\n=\\int_0^22t\\sqrt{t^2+8}\\,dt.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns =\\int_0^22t\\sqrt{t^2+8}\\,dt\n=\\left[\\frac23(t^2+8)^{3/2}\\right]_0^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =16\\sqrt3-\\frac{32\\sqrt2}{3}\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by the parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=5(1+t)^{1/2},\\quad y=5(1-t)^{1/2}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the exact length of the arc of the curve between the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5\\sqrt2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac52(1+t)^{-1/2},\\qquad\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-\\frac52(1-t)^{-1/2}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2\n=\\frac{25}{4(1+t)}+\\frac{25}{4(1-t)}\n=\\frac{25}{2(1-t^2)}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The arc length is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^1\\frac{5\\sqrt2}{2\\sqrt{1-t^2}}\\,dt\n=\\frac{5\\sqrt2}{2}[\\arcsin t]_0^1\n=\\frac{5\\sqrt2\\pi}{4}\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>A circle has parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=r\\cos\\theta\\quad\\text{and}\\quad y=r\\sin\\theta.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>By finding the arc length of the curve from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, show that the length of the circumference is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi r\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=r\\cos\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=r\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dx}{d\\theta}=-r\\sin\\theta,\\qquad\n\\frac{dy}{d\\theta}=r\\cos\\theta.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus the speed is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{dx}{d\\theta}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{d\\theta}\\right)^2}\n=\\sqrt{r^2(\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta)}=r.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^{2\\pi}r\\,d\\theta=2\\pi r.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q19","number":19,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by the parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=2+e^{-t}(\\cos t+\\sin t),\\quad y=1+e^{-t}(\\cos t-\\sin t)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the exact length of the arc of the curve between the points where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>Differentiating the parametric equations,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=-2e^{-t}\\sin t,\\qquad\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-2e^{-t}\\cos t.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore the speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2e^{-t}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^32e^{-t}\\,dt=[-2e^{-t}]_0^3=2-\\frac2{e^3}\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q20","number":20,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by the parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=2+3\\cos t,\\quad y=3t+3\\sin t\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2=36\\cos^2\\left(\\frac t2\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence find the exact length of the curve between the points that occur when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=-3\\sin t,\\qquad \\frac{dy}{dt}=3+3\\cos t.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2\n =9\\sin^2t+9(1+\\cos t)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =18(1+\\cos t)=36\\cos^2\\left(\\frac t2\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos(t/2)\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^\\pi6\\cos\\left(\\frac t2\\right)dt\n=\\left[12\\sin\\left(\\frac t2\\right)\\right]_0^\\pi\n=12\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q21","number":21,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by the parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=3\\sin^3t,\\quad y=3\\cos^3t\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t&lt;2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the exact length of the arc of the curve between the points where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=9\\sin^2t\\cos t,\\qquad\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-9\\cos^2t\\sin t.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2\n =81\\sin^2t\\cos^2t(\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac{81}{4}\\sin^2(2t).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq\\pi/2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac92\\sin2t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\frac92\\sin2t\\,dt=\\frac92\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q22","number":22,"question":"<p>A curve is defined by the parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=4\\sin t-\\sin4t,\\quad y=4\\cos t-\\cos4t\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2=64\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{3t}{2}\\right)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence find the exact length of the curve between the points that occur when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\frac\\pi3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=4\\cos t-4\\cos4t,\\qquad\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=-4\\sin t+4\\sin4t.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos A\\cos B+\\sin A\\sin B=\\cos(A-B)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2\n =16+16-32\\cos(4t-t)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =32(1-\\cos3t)=64\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{3t}{2}\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq\\pi/3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin(3t/2)\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^{\\pi/3}8\\sin\\left(\\frac{3t}{2}\\right)dt\n=\\left[-\\frac{16}{3}\\cos\\left(\\frac{3t}{2}\\right)\\right]_0^{\\pi/3}\n=\\frac{16}{3}\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q23","number":23,"question":"<p>A designer models the shape of a curved skateboard ramp using parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=k(t+\\sin t),\\quad y=k(1-\\cos t)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are measured in metres, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive constant. The ramp section runs from the ground at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the platform at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Given the exact length of the ramp between the ground and the ramp is 12 metres, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <strong>Prerequisite Knowledge for Question 24: Calculus of Hyperbolic Functions</strong></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=k(1+\\cos t),\\qquad \\frac{dy}{dt}=k\\sin t.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2\n=k^2(2+2\\cos t)=4k^2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac t2\\right).\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq t\\leq\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k\\cos(t/2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^\\pi2k\\cos\\left(\\frac t2\\right)dt=4k.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q24","number":24,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>By using the substitution <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\sinh x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int\\operatorname{sech}x\\,dx=\\arctan(\\sinh x)+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol><p>A curve is defined by the parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=\\operatorname{sech}t,\\quad y=\\tanh t\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>[b)] Find the exact length of the arc of the curve between the points where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=\\ln2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u=\\sinh x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"du=\\cosh x\\,dx\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cosh^2x=1+u^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\operatorname{sech}x\\,dx\n=\\int\\frac{du}{1+u^2}\n=\\arctan u+c\n=\\arctan(\\sinh x)+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=-\\tanh t\\,\\operatorname{sech}t,\\qquad\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=\\operatorname{sech}^2t.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tanh^2t+\\operatorname{sech}^2t=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\operatorname{sech}t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns=\\int_0^{\\ln2}\\operatorname{sech}t\\,dt\n=[\\arctan(\\sinh t)]_0^{\\ln2}\n=\\arctan\\frac34\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core2-2.37-q25","number":25,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\sqrt{1+x^2}\\,dx=\\frac12x\\sqrt{x^2+1}+\\frac12\\ln\\left(x+\\sqrt{x^2+1}\\right)+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span></li></ol><p>A curve is defined by the parametric equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nx=at^2,\\quad y=4at\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a positive constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>[b)] Find the exact length of the arc of the curve between the points where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\sinh u\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"dx=\\cosh u\\,du\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{1+x^2}=\\cosh u\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Then</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\int\\sqrt{1+x^2}\\,dx\n =\\int\\cosh^2u\\,du\n=\\frac14\\sinh2u+\\frac12u+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac12x\\sqrt{x^2+1}+\\frac12\\operatorname{arsinh}x+c\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac12x\\sqrt{x^2+1}+\\frac12\\ln\\left(x+\\sqrt{x^2+1}\\right)+c.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=2at,\\qquad \\frac{dy}{dt}=4a,\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so the speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2a\\sqrt{t^2+4}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\ns =\\int_0^12a\\sqrt{t^2+4}\\,dt\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =a\\left[t\\sqrt{t^2+4}+4\\ln\\left(t+\\sqrt{t^2+4}\\right)\\right]_0^1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =a\\left(\\sqrt5+4\\ln\\frac{1+\\sqrt5}{2}\\right)\\text{ units}.\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]}]